{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-jacobi-field","title":"def:pet-ch3-jacobi-field","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.md","line":529,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex#def:pet-ch3-jacobi-field","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex","label":"def:pet-ch3-jacobi-field","line":1004,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Jacobi field]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch3-jacobi-field}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0116}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation}\n\n  For a smooth distance function $r$, a \\emph{Jacobi field} is a smooth vector\n  field $J$ independent of $r$, i.e.\\ satisfying the \\emph{Jacobi equation}\n  $\\mathcal L_{\\partial_r}J=0$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Jacobi field] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368332d6a61636f62692d6669656c64\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0116</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-distance-function-notation\">↗ def:pet-ch3-distance-function-notation</a> <p></p>For a smooth distance function <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r$\">$r$</span>, a <em>Jacobi field</em> is a smooth vector field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J$\">$J$</span> independent of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r$\">$r$</span>, i.e. satisfying the <em>Jacobi equation</em> <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"fal